---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
const shared = [
  { k: "britain", n: "D’Arcy", w: "England & Ireland, back to a General born in 1751" },
  { k: "italy",   n: "Falco",  w: "Arienzo, back to a priest’s pen in 1767" },
];
const theirs = [
  { k: "croatia",   n: "Defranceski", w: "Croatia" },
  { k: "blazevic",  n: "Blažević",    w: "Croatia" },
  { k: "argentina", n: "Lerena",      w: "Argentina" },
  { k: "safrica",   n: "Booyzen",     w: "South Africa" },
];
const mazza = [
  { k: "mazza",     n: "Mazza",     w: "Sicily" },
  { k: "prostamo",  n: "Prostamo",  w: "Calabria" },
  { k: "arena",     n: "Arena",     w: "Calabria" },
  { k: "polistena", n: "Polistena", w: "Calabria" },
];
---
<Base title="Cousins" dek="Four cousins, ten families. Half of each cousin's family tree is identical to the other's, and half has nothing in common at all.">
  <div class="hero" style="text-align:left">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="kicker" style="--c:var(--safrica)">Four of you</div>
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(36px,6.4vw,66px)">You and your cousins</h1>
      <p class="lead big">Alessio and Mateo have two cousins, Rocco and Mia. Half of your family
      tree is <em>exactly</em> the same as theirs. The other half has nothing in common at all.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Why? Because your mums are twins</h2>
      <p class="lead">Two sisters, born on the same day. One of them married Alessio and Mateo’s
      dad. The other married Rocco and Mia’s dad. That one fact is the reason for everything on
      this page.</p>
      <div class="cousinsplit">
        <div class="csplit c-mazza">
          <b>Rocco &amp; Mia</b>
          <span>MRM + SFD</span>
          <div class="cchips">{mazza.map(f => <a class={`cchip c-${f.k}`} href={u(`/${f.n.toLowerCase()}/`)}>{f.n}<i>{f.w}</i></a>)}</div>
        </div>
        <div class="csplit shared">
          <b>Shared by all four</b>
          <span>Grandpa IKD + Grandma GF</span>
          <div class="cchips">{shared.map(f => <a class={`cchip c-${f.k}`} href={u(`/${f.n === "D’Arcy" ? "darcy" : "falco"}/`)}>{f.n}<i>{f.w}</i></a>)}</div>
        </div>
        <div class="csplit c-croatia">
          <b>Alessio &amp; Mateo</b>
          <span>DID + CAD</span>
          <div class="cchips">{theirs.map(f => <a class={`cchip c-${f.k}`} href={u(`/${f.n === "Blažević" ? "blazevic" : f.n.toLowerCase()}/`)}>{f.n}<i>{f.w}</i></a>)}</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="kicker" style="--c:var(--safrica)">What that means</div>
      <h2>Same grandma, same grandpa — and then nothing</h2>
      <div class="grid g2" style="margin-top:24px">
        <div class="callout" style="--c:var(--britain);--cw:var(--britain-wash);--cd:var(--britain-deep)">
          <h3>The half you share</h3>
          <p>All four of you have the same grandma and grandpa on your mother’s side. So the D’Arcy
          family and the Falco family belong to every one of you — the soldier who guarded the
          convict ship, the surveyor who helped map Melbourne, the parrot that shouted “Come in!”,
          the falcon the Falcos are named after, and the priest at Arienzo in 1767. All four of you,
          equally.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="callout" style="--c:var(--mazza);--cw:var(--mazza-wash);--cd:var(--mazza-deep)">
          <h3>The half you don’t</h3>
          <p>On your fathers’ sides you have <b>nothing whatsoever</b> in common. Alessio and Mateo’s
          dad brings four families from Croatia, Argentina and South Africa — three continents.
          Rocco and Mia’s dad brings four families from Sicily and Calabria — three towns in the
          south of Italy. Not one name overlaps.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="kicker" style="--c:var(--safrica)">Things worth knowing</div>
      <h2>Three facts from your cousins’ side</h2>
      <div class="grid g3" style="margin-top:24px">
        <div class="jobcard c-arena">
          <div class="jt">Three Roccos</div>
          <p>Rocco is named for his dad, Michael <b>Rocco</b> Mazza, who is named for <i>his</i>
          grandfather Rocco Arena, born at Scilla in 1924.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="jobcard c-prostamo">
          <div class="jt">1697</div>
          <p>The Prostamo line goes back nine generations — older than anybody on Alessio and
          Mateo’s side. And it arrives through a great-grandmother, not the surname.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="jobcard c-mazza">
          <div class="jt">Four graves in a row</div>
          <p>Rocco and Mia’s four Italian great-grandparents lie in consecutive plots at Nudgee in
          Brisbane, buried in the order they died — nineteen years between the first and the last.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pager">
        <a href={u("/")}>🌳 The whole tree</a>
        <a href="https://daviddef.github.io/TheMazza/">The Mazza Archive →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
